00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.720
when a criminal lawyer just tries to confuse&nbsp;
the jury instead of refuting the case. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:46.720
reason that this can work in criminal trials is&nbsp;
we have the standard of reasonable doubt. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.960
if a defense attorney can introduce reasonable&nbsp;
doubt, any kind of reasonable doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.920
then they are a significant step closer to&nbsp;
securing an acquittal for their client. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.960
so the idea of a Chewbacca defense would be&nbsp;
a prosecution comes together and makes a case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:09.040
that's relevant and it's germane to the facts&nbsp;
and the complaint that is being adjudicated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:17.680
And a defense attorney can introduce irrelevant&nbsp;
facts, stories, confusion. And if you can get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.280
the jurors just saying, well, we had the case from&nbsp;
the prosecution and then we had the case from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.080
defense, even if the case from the defense&nbsp;
was irrelevant and didn't make any sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:33.760
if it makes the jurors feel as though there's&nbsp;
some kind of doubt as to what happened, even if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.360
it's because the defense lawyer was talking about&nbsp;
Chewbacca, Star Wars, vinyl records and whatever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.760
you can turn what might be a very good case for&nbsp;
the prosecution into a confusing enough case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.360
that maybe you get a juror to say, I think we've&nbsp;
got to go with not guilty because I'm still even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:54.240
confused about what it is that took place. That's&nbsp;
the that's the idea of the Chewbacca defense.&nbsp;

